{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03041",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.17,
      "end_seconds": 6.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.67,
      "end_seconds": 15.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Afternoon, uh, is this seat fine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.91,
      "end_seconds": 19.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "What's the main thing today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.81,
      "end_seconds": 21.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "I've been feeling faint."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.87,
      "end_seconds": 31.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.94,
      "end_seconds": 37.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "It's, It's moderate, honestly. I'd say once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.28,
      "end_seconds": 41.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Alright, any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.77,
      "end_seconds": 48.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get breathlessness as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.78,
      "end_seconds": 53.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.97,
      "end_seconds": 57.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.55,
      "end_seconds": 62.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. So, have you had a gurgling chest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.3,
      "end_seconds": 64.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yeah, that too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.77,
      "end_seconds": 69.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Have you noticed chest pain, fever or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.57,
      "end_seconds": 74.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Erm, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.23,
      "end_seconds": 78.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.78,
      "end_seconds": 80.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.83,
      "end_seconds": 85.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.88,
      "end_seconds": 87.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.52,
      "end_seconds": 94.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.61,
      "end_seconds": 97.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "My son has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.76,
      "end_seconds": 110.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.1,
      "end_seconds": 116.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Yes, thin bones. I've been putting this off for weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.15,
      "end_seconds": 119.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.0,
      "end_seconds": 139.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Alright, and alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.87,
      "end_seconds": 145.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.95,
      "end_seconds": 146.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.79,
      "end_seconds": 150.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.37,
      "end_seconds": 154.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.19,
      "end_seconds": 159.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.97,
      "end_seconds": 162.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.85,
      "end_seconds": 169.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.45,
      "end_seconds": 173.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.11,
      "end_seconds": 176.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.13,
      "end_seconds": 180.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.69,
      "end_seconds": 186.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Ah, it's alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.4,
      "end_seconds": 201.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.99,
      "end_seconds": 206.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "No, you know, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.37,
      "end_seconds": 210.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.59,
      "end_seconds": 219.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Okay, keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.58,
      "end_seconds": 251.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 103, blood pressure 135 over 74, SpO2 94 percent on room air. And respiratory rate 24, temperature 37.4."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.36,
      "end_seconds": 255.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Is that alright, uh, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.64,
      "end_seconds": 269.9,
      "duration_seconds": 13.26,
      "text": "Okay, we'll look at it together shortly. So, based on your history, my working impression is life-threatening haemoptysis. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.94,
      "end_seconds": 273.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.44,
      "end_seconds": 306.24,
      "duration_seconds": 30.8,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like life-threatening haemoptysis, but I'd like to confirm. Let's book urgent blood tests to look into bleeding. I want an urgent CT scan done, that's for massive haemoptysis. We'll begin with tranexamic acid, 1 gram, now, single dose. It's for haemoptysis. Lie on the bleeding side and I am calling the emergency team. Let's get you seen by the emergency team, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.75,
      "end_seconds": 308.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.41,
      "end_seconds": 325.92,
      "duration_seconds": 15.51,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like to see you again straight away. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.94,
      "end_seconds": 332.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}